target/
*.class
.env

# Pen-test / SCA scratch. None of these are build output — they are the scan's
# own working dirs, and every one of them is created INSIDE the checkout:
#   .dep-check-data/  Makefile pentest-sca USE_DOCKER=1 NVD database mount
#   .nvd-cache/       --data dir for the CI SCA scans (.gitlab-ci.yml pentest:sca
#                     and the `sca` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml)
#   reports/          dependency-check --out (HTML/SARIF/JSON)
#   out/pentest/      PENTEST_REPORTS for the shared DAST harness
# Left untracked-but-unignored they show up as a dirty tree, which matters here:
# .gitlab-ci.yml's `test` job ends in `git diff --exit-code` to catch a build that
# rewrites a committed artefact, and scan scratch must not be able to muddy that.
# Anchored with a leading `/`: unanchored, `reports/` would also hide any
# directory named `reports` anywhere under src/, which is not what this block
# says it does — every path here is created at the repo ROOT.
/.dep-check-data/
/.nvd-cache/
/reports/
/out/pentest/
